* Any serious infection other than chronic hepatitis B infection requires intravenous anti-infective therapy;
* HCV RNA positive, HIV antibody positive, syphilis positive within 12 months;
* Abnormal laboratory results;
* Diseases associated with vascular inflammatory conditions;
* QT interval corrected heart rate (Fridericia method) abnormal;
* History of malignancy or ongoing assessment of possible malignancy;
* History of allergies, or allergic constitution;
* Recent major trauma or major surgery, or planned surgery;
