Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients with indication of asymptomatic bilateral extractions of lower third molars;
* Aged 18 years or older;
* Have a good health and no disease;

Exclusion Criteria:

* Patients with history of any medication treatment within 15 days before the beginning of the research, history of allergy to the drugs, substances or materials used in this study, pregnancy or lactation.

Inclusion Criteria:

1. patients aged 18-75years,
2. patients with gastric cancer confirmed by histology or cytology at first visit,
3. patients with advanced tumor by imaging evaluation,
4. patients with preoperative neoadjuvant therapy;
5. Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) physical status score of 0 or 1;
6. tolerance to chemotherapy in laboratory examination;
